# Guest image artifacts. One `<sha256>  <url>  <role>` line per artifact; `#`
# starts a comment and the role defaults to `rootfs`.
#
# The build FAILS CLOSED: a line without a 64-char checksum, an unknown role, or
# a download whose hash does not match stops it. Nothing else may enter the
# image — this file is the whole supply chain for the guest rootfs.
#
# Roles:
#   rootfs   extracted into the guest rootfs (both tiers)
#   dev      a package `apk add --root`ed into the rootfs, dev tier only
#
# The `dev` set is the RESOLVED CLOSURE of git/nodejs/npm/python3/rust/cargo/zig
# as apk resolved it against the v3.24 branch on 2026-10-18, frozen here package
# by package: apk resolves dependencies across the whole set, so a partial list
# fails to install. Re-pin by re-running scripts/resolve-guest-packages.sh in
# the builder container and reviewing every line — the image hash is the image
# version, so a re-pin is a NEW image, never a mutation of this one.
#
# Alpine minirootfs is musl end to end, which is why it works in a guest with no
# glibc: busybox is the shell and the coreutils (304 applets), and `apk` adds the
# dev toolchain from the same released generation.
#
# Version pinning: `/alpine/v3.24/...` is an immutable released-branch path and a
# published `.apk` is never rewritten. Never use latest-stable here.
c5ca053cfe1d85c5b96dff8b9bc57045f7f184a30ffb6b65776409ca90388677  https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/v3.24/releases/x86_64/alpine-minirootfs-3.24.2-x86_64.tar.gz  rootfs

